<title>USA: US ITC - 1 MB drams from S.Korea being dumped in US.</title>
<headline>US ITC - 1 MB drams from S.Korea being dumped in US.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. International Trade Commission said Wednesday imports of dynamic random access memory chips of one megabit or above from South Korea were being sold in the U.S. at less than fair value.</p>
<p>The federal agency also said in a statement that as a result of this, U.S. industry was being or was threatened with being materially injured.</p>
<p>It said the 3-1 vote by ITC commissioners was in response to a remand order from the Court of International Trade, which in turn was responding to an appeal of the ITC's original May 1993 finding to the same effect.</p>
</text>
